WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:01.810
Quack!

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:05.060
Dante. Dominique's not with you?

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:06.190
What? Domi?

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:08.980
Aw, hell. I thought you might be on to us.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.320
Anyone who didn't notice that
needs their head examined.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:13.990
I won't argue that.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:18.160
But enough about that, quack!
Some unbelievable info just came in!

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.200
The Beast lives!

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.450
The Beast of Gévaudan

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:24.960
has reared its head!

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.210
Now that's interesting.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:32.590
Don't spare the details, Dante.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.850
We'll take this to Gévaudan.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.310
Pardon me.

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:44.730
No need.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:49.480
It was entirely my fault, monsieur.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.650
Noé, over here.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.530
Wait for me, Vanitas!

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:34.210
"The Case Study of Vanitas"

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:45.560
"Dear Teacher, I hope
this letter finds you well.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.140
I have left Paris along with Vanitas

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:52.900
and traveled to the
faraway region of Gévaudan."

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.610
Vanitas, look!

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:56.730
There's a village!

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:59.110
Is that Saugues?

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.700
It's so beautiful.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:06.290
It somehow reminds me of Averoigne.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.250
Hey, Noé.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.580
Why have you been so chipper
since we boarded this wagon?

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.750
Me? Why have <i>you</i> looked
like you're on death's door?

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.250
I'm freezing!

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:18.960
Hmph, that's just sad.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:23.300
Shut it. Unlike you people,
I'm a highly sensitive person.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:27.640
And what are you information
peddlers doing here anyway?

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.520
Who cares? It's no skin off your nose.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:33.730
We just want to collect
information we can sell.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.150
Precisely.

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:39.190
And then there was that
thing with the Chasseurs.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.990
I wasn't satisfied

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:46.580
till I clobbered those enhanced humans or
whatever they were that worked me over.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:49.950
Oh, Dante, you're so sweet.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:55.750
You wanted to murder that
heinous villain who broke my arm?

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:59.210
No doubt they're here
to gather information,

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:02.130
but they likely have
ulterior motives as well.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:07.180
We'll stow our things at the inn,
then head to where the bodies were found.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:11.600
I want to look for signs
of the Beast before dark.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:13.190
Of course.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:21.860
Here in Gévaudan in the 18th century,

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:26.370
the Beast brutally ripped over
100 women and children to shreds.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:30.450
Its large maw was twisted,
and its ears pointed.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.370
It had sharp claws and
a body covered in red fur.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.790
It is said to have
resembled an enormous wolf.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:40.920
Is there really such a beast
here in the Silver Forest?

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.380
It's not just the Beast.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:43.260
What?

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:49.180
A witch of tremendous power
is also said to dwell here.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:50.890
A witch?

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.640
Vanitas, you believe the Beast of Gévaudan

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:56.980
may very well be a
curse-bearing vampire, don't you?

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:58.900
So the legends say.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:03.780
Then I imagine that curse-bearer and
witch must be connected in some manner.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.110
Who knows?

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:11.370
All I can say is there may be a
curse-bearer, and that's why I'm here.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:15.960
Wh-What was that creepy sound?!

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:19.250
I believe that was a bird.

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.550
The scent of the forest air

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.210
brings back memories.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:26.590
Domi and I used to play
in the forest all the time.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:28.340
Tree nuts!

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:29.800
Stick close to me.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:33.470
Look, Vanitas.
They're the kind you can eat!

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:40.650
Hmph, you're having
more fun than I thought.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:41.520
What?

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.400
With him.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:44.820
You being who you are,

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:49.910
I thought you two would go your
separate ways when things went south.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:55.790
I tried, but that fool was waiting
when I tried to give him the slip.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:58.080
What's this?

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:00.630
Your special someone is the heroic type?

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:02.880
I <i>will</i> murder you, baldy!

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:09.800
Johann, don't let Noé out of your sight.

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:12.350
He'll vanish the moment
you're not looking.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:16.350
I know. He vanished just like that!
It's quite impressive.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:19.230
Noé!

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:23.360
I'm so glad I found it.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:27.190
Bad Murr! We must stick with the others!

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:31.280
Huh?

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:38.370
They're all gone, just like that.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:42.750
Could this be the power
of the woods witch?

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:49.510
Oh my, dear Noé's nowhere to be found.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:03.980
Snow?

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:08.610
What the devil?! It's freezing!

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:11.030
Oh no, Dante. This is <i>not</i> good.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:16.160
Sweet Vanitas isn't breathing!

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:20.040
Hey, Quack! Snap out of it!

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.620
Quiet! Someone's coming.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:23.830
A trespasser?

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:24.840
Yes, sir.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:29.550
She claims to be with the Church,
but something doesn't seem right.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:32.340
I'm on my way to report
it to Monsieur Antoine.

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.550
Forget about trespassers.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:36.310
Find the Beast now!

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:41.600
We shall slay the fiend and present
its corpse before His Majesty!

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.980
What's with their getup?

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:45.900
Who's "His Majesty"?

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:47.900
They're dragoons.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.900
During the 18th century attacks,

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:54.820
King Louis XV ordered his dragoons
to investigate sightings of the Beast.

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:59.080
Antoine was the name of
the king's First Musketeer.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.750
What? Hold on.

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:05.330
You make it sound like
we traveled back in time.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:10.710
It seems fate has dealt us a vexing hand.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:16.510
What's that?

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.350
I don't like this!

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:42.040
There it is.

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:44.670
It's here!

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:47.000
The Beast of Gévaudan!

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:50.590
What the hell?!
No one said it was <i>that</i> big!

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.430
Did they kill it?!

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:58.680
No.

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:13.400
Guns don't kill it?

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.700
It heals too fast.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.660
A red-eyed beast.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:18.820
A woods witch.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:20.740
The 18th-century killings.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:23.000
The rewinding of time.

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:25.330
We're in the past?

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:27.790
If not, then what?

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:30.500
A malnomen? But which one?!

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:33.420
The devil take him!

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:35.670
Why'd he have to vanish now?!

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:38.470
Where is that idiot?!

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:48.560
Jeanne?

00:09:57.740 --> 00:09:59.820
H-Help!

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.870
What's this?

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.770
I remember you.

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:28.350
Did we not meet at the station in Paris?

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:29.980
Who <i>are</i> you?

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:31.940
My name is Astolfo.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:36.820
I am the 12th Paladin and have been
honored with the title of Garnet.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:39.660
Pleased to meet you, monsieur.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:43.120
Why did you kill him?

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:45.160
You're a Chasseur.

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:46.290
So why kill humans--

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:50.040
These men mistook me for a woman.

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:51.130
What?

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:54.880
What's more, they would
not listen to a word I said.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:58.670
I warned them three times,
yet they still laid hands upon me.

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:03.600
In short, it was an act of self-defense.

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:06.270
Also, you seem to be mistaken.

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:10.640
Protecting humans is not part
of a Chasseur's job description.

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:13.440
We hunt vampires.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:17.400
Have I made myself clear, monsieur?

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:21.820
Eyes of red.

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:23.990
I wasn't sure till now.

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:25.950
You're a vampire!

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:33.330
What is the matter?
Why don't you fight back?

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.170
He enjoys this.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:38.550
The battle, the bloodshed.

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:47.100
He's nothing like Roland
and the other Chasseurs!

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.100
He's still alive.

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:58.570
Bah! You were not satisfied
with simply impeding my work?

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:02.030
Now you wish to spoil my fun?

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:05.240
That I cannot forgive.

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:08.490
You deserve 10,000 deaths.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:13.000
What is...

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:17.460
What is wrong with you?!

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:21.170
Ready to fight now, are we?

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:25.590
Take that!

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:36.770
Now my Louisette shall claim your head!

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:45.950
Noé!

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:52.370
You all right, chum?

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:55.000
There you are, Sweet Noé!

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:58.880
Jeanne, wait!
Don't kill the Beast, not yet!

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:02.210
I must do this.

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:07.300
I failed to slay you here
in Gévaudan so long ago.

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:11.220
Now die!

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:25.490
Jeanne?! Why is <i>she</i> here?

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:28.780
The Beast of Gévaudan.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:32.450
And that vampire. Could it truly be...

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:34.750
...the Hellfire Witch?!

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:39.460
What a splendid day this is!

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:42.920
To think I'd bear witness
to not only the Beast,

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:45.550
but Lord Ruthven's bourreau, too!

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:49.680
Stay still, Noé. Your wounds will--

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:52.600
No, I have some fight left in me.

00:13:57.140 --> 00:14:00.360
I have a score to settle with him.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:02.190
Unknot your knickers.

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:05.740
What?

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:09.320
That little runt is formidable?

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:10.740
Even more than Roland?

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:12.490
No way in hell!

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:14.410
Roland was far more terrifying!

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:16.910
That kid has nothing on him!

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:19.790
Then why are you all beat up?

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:25.800
Did you believe he would
listen to reason like Roland?

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:31.430
Or did you hold back because
he seemed more like a little girl?

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:33.180
Listen to me, Noé.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:38.390
You're all worked up, and it's keeping you
from performing at your usual level.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:44.230
I'm the right man for the job.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:51.740
Here is the proper course of action!

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:56.120
What?! A Chasseur paladin is here?!

00:14:56.120 --> 00:15:02.000
C-C-Could it be Roland the Jasper?!

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.630
What? It's not?

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:05.840
It's Astolfo the Garnet?

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:07.090
Who the heck is that?

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:10.510
Sorry, never heard of him!

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:13.430
But what a relief!

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:17.520
We'd have been as good as dead
if it had been Roland the Jasper!

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:20.890
But we might have a chance
against a little girl!

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:22.900
This really is good news!

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:24.360
What? You're kidding?

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:28.940
He's a boy? Seriously?! No way!

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:34.200
Roland?

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:38.040
Are you saying that
buffoon is better than me?

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:39.200
That was easy.

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:41.420
Um, Vanitas?

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:44.250
That is my specialty.

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:46.630
You stop Jeanne.

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:50.880
If the Beast truly is a curse-bearer
that has changed form,

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:53.800
its malnomen has yet to be discovered.

00:15:53.800 --> 00:16:00.140
We can't have anyone slaying it,
whether they be a Chasseur or a bourreau.

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:03.020
I'm here to save vampires.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:04.810
Aren't you?

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:09.320
You know

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:11.650
I am!

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:15.370
Chloé! I know it's you!

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:16.780
Chloé!

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:25.540
This time, I <i>will</i> slay you!

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:31.510
You mustn't.

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:32.720
Noé?

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:34.430
Please, Jeanne.

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:37.930
Don't slay the Beast. Not yet.

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:40.180
You must know by now.

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:50.320
Vanitas may be able
to save that curse-bearer.

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:53.200
Save her?

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:55.950
I cannot allow that.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:17:00.240
I'm here as a bourreau. It is my
duty to execute curse-bearers.

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:03.580
And if you insist on impeding me,

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:06.040
I will slay you, too!

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:08.500
What? Is that all you've got?

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:11.590
The Chasseurs must really be shorthanded

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:14.090
if they're hiring such
boneheaded paladins.

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:17.550
But that's not it, is it?

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:20.600
In your case, your family
connections got you in,

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:23.390
Astolfo Granatum.

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:27.440
I hear the ties are strong between
House Granatum and the Church.

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:30.690
You must have begged your
father to get where you are.

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:35.280
"Please, Daddy. I really
wanna be a paladin."

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:38.820
"Isn't there something you could do?"

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:41.580
Come on, I'm dying to know.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:47.540
How much did it cost Daddy to buy
your seat at the paladin table?

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:52.960
Don't you dare denigrate my father!

00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:59.680
How delightful.

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:02.890
How very delightful!

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:07.100
Would you mind?

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:13.650
May I join the fun?

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:17.860
What's that?!

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:39.800
Charlatan.

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:47.980
So, we meet again, Noé.

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:49.810
Naenia.

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:55.860
Wh-What in heaven's name is this?

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:59.030
Big Brother, help me.

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:01.240
Big Brother.

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:03.080
Big Brother.

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:24.510
Dante, don't get drawn into their world!

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:29.810
The Beast is gone.

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:31.600
Where could it be?

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:41.610
Jeanne, our darling daughter.

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:51.830
I will kill you.

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:54.840
You and every last vampire.

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:57.500
I'll slaughter all of you!

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:14.770
I'm sick of this.

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:30.250
Let's put an end to
this revolting spectacle.

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:35.140
There you are.

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:39.860
Let us return to the castle, Chloé.

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:53.290
My leg hurts too much to walk.

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:57.250
Carry me.

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:05.010
"A Chance Encounter"

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:39.940
"The Witch and the Young Man"
